1
00:00:00,210 --> 00:00:02,180
A Harbor board reviewer asks Morgan a

2
00:00:02,220 --> 00:00:04,220
fair question: what happens when the

3
00:00:04,270 --> 00:00:06,360
preparation agent produces a brief that

4
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:08,880
looks ready, but the evidence is thin?

5
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:11,310
Morgan brings three paper panels to the

6
00:00:11,350 --> 00:00:11,790
table.

7
00:00:12,209 --> 00:00:15,793
The first panel shows the queue, including held and rejected work.

8
00:00:16,347 --> 00:00:18,566
The second follows one item through its trace.

9
00:00:19,121 --> 00:00:21,041
The third shows the rule that governed it.

10
00:00:21,553 --> 00:00:24,753
This is a design walkthrough, not a live system demonstration.

11
00:00:25,206 --> 00:00:28,960
Morgan is showing what Harbor intends to inspect before it trusts the workflow.

12
00:00:29,302 --> 00:00:29,942
Start with the queue.

13
00:00:30,326 --> 00:00:33,654
One Session Option Brief is prepared, not proposed to the team.

14
00:00:34,123 --> 00:00:36,384
The staffing hold says staffing is unconfirmed.

15
00:00:36,956 --> 00:00:38,961
The print request says no spend is approved.

16
00:00:39,473 --> 00:00:43,484
The research proposal is not run because its baseline and reviewer protocol are missing.

17
00:00:44,252 --> 00:00:46,513
Place the rejections where the reviewer can see them too.

18
00:00:47,011 --> 00:00:52,302
A queue that only displays polished outputs hides the decisions that make the operation governable.

19
00:00:52,814 --> 00:00:54,521
Open the trace for the held brief.

20
00:00:54,990 --> 00:00:57,251
It begins with cleared Harbor source references.

21
00:00:57,922 --> 00:01:04,962
It records the preparation agent's draft, the check that found the staffing gap, the hold, and Morgan as the decision owner.

22
00:01:05,687 --> 00:01:07,308
There is no send or booking event.

23
00:01:07,884 --> 00:01:15,223
The trace should let someone ask why the item stopped, without exposing raw source notes or pretending a paper receipt is a live audit log.

24
00:01:15,863 --> 00:01:17,783
The absence of an event is part of the answer.

25
00:01:18,338 --> 00:01:19,276
Now show memory.

26
00:01:19,851 --> 00:01:26,593
Harbor has a proposed local rule: a session cannot move from option to team proposal until a person confirms staffing.

27
00:01:27,062 --> 00:01:30,561
In this classroom design, that rule is a draft for Morgan's review.

28
00:01:31,312 --> 00:01:36,901
The agent cannot promote it itself, and a single held example cannot become general truth by repetition.

29
00:01:37,626 --> 00:01:42,149
Show the rule's owner, scope, source reference, status, and review date.

30
00:01:42,405 --> 00:01:44,197
If any are missing, say so.

31
00:01:44,726 --> 00:01:47,628
The workbook asks what export a reviewer can take away.

32
00:01:48,054 --> 00:01:53,516
Morgan can offer the scoped proof outline from lesson twelve after a separate audience and privacy review.

33
00:01:54,229 --> 00:01:59,007
It would contain the boundary, receipt references, decisions, and limitations.

34
00:01:59,690 --> 00:02:02,250
It would omit raw notes and unrelated records.

35
00:02:02,847 --> 00:02:04,895
For class today, it stays `not shared`.

36
00:02:05,364 --> 00:02:07,839
A reviewer may ask whether the agent actually ran.

37
00:02:08,367 --> 00:02:09,624
Answer plainly: no.

38
00:02:09,775 --> 00:02:14,895
This exercise demonstrates controls on paper; it does not prove production reliability.

39
00:02:15,407 --> 00:02:15,869
Pause.

40
00:02:16,054 --> 00:02:20,015
Which panel would expose the weakest part of your own proposed workflow first?

41
00:02:20,713 --> 00:02:23,017
Storyboard a Three-Panel Demo for your workflow.

42
00:02:23,444 --> 00:02:26,601
Give each panel a reviewer question and one piece of evidence.

43
00:02:27,113 --> 00:02:30,185
Include a blocked or rejected item beside the successful work.

44
00:02:30,807 --> 00:02:34,647
In the trace, name the missing event as clearly as the recorded ones.

45
00:02:35,202 --> 00:02:37,719
In memory, identify who may approve the rule.

46
00:02:38,189 --> 00:02:41,218
Write two likely skeptical questions and honest answers.

47
00:02:41,830 --> 00:02:47,462
Decide what a reviewer may receive, what stays withheld, and who reviews the export before sharing.

48
00:02:47,889 --> 00:02:49,809
Use a fictional or approved example.

49
00:02:50,449 --> 00:03:37,412
Do not use private operational data.

50
00:03:37,924 --> 00:03:39,886
Save revision fourteen as a draft.

51
00:03:40,539 --> 00:03:44,294
The board can examine Harbor's proposed controls and its unresolved gaps.

52
00:03:45,147 --> 00:03:46,854
Morgan still owns the session decision.

53
00:03:47,397 --> 00:03:49,957
Nothing about a clean storyboard lifts

54
00:03:49,997 --> 00:03:50,687
the hold.
